{
 "state": "WY",
 "file": "Social-Studies-Standards-20142018-additions_FINAL_f5341c.pdf",
 "structure": "Wyoming Social Studies Content and Performance Standards 2014 with 2018 additions. Front matter (cover, acknowledgments, rationale, 2018 American Indian additions rationale, organization, cross-curricular codes), then six Content Standards (1 Citizenship, Government, and Democracy; 2 Culture and Cultural Diversity; 3 Production, Distribution, and Consumption; 4 Time, Continuity, and Change; 5 People, Places, and Environments; 6 Technology, Literacy, and Global Connections). Each has a heading with description, a Rationale, a 'Benchmarks Students will:' table spread over several pages with four columns C1=End of Grade 2 (K-2 band), C2=End of Grade 5 (3-5), C3=End of Grade 8 (6-8), C4=Upon Graduation/Grade 12 (9-12); table rows give benchmarks coded SSg.s.n (g=2,5,8,12; s=standard; n=benchmark) and 2018 additions coded with a suffix (e.g. SS8.1.1.a), plus ELA/health/CV cross-curricular codes appended in the cell. Strand labels in standard 5 (Spatial; Physical Place and Region; Human Place and Movement; Environment and Society) appear as cells in each column. Then Performance Level Descriptors per content standard by grade 2, 5, 8, 12 (Advanced/Proficient/Basic/Below Basic). Back matter: glossary with examples, historical background, references, committee lists.",
